  "preamble": "Assibilation of the palatalized velar [kʲ] to the alveolar fricative [s] is the classic satem outcome of the Proto-Indo-European palatovelar *ḱ, conventionally interpreted as a palatalized velar. Armenian shows *ḱ > s directly (*ḱḗrdi- > sirt 'heart', *déḱm̥ > tasn 'ten'), and Slavic has s in the same words (*ḱm̥tóm > OCS съто, Russian сто 'hundred'), where Balto-Slavic is usually reconstructed with an intermediate *ś on the evidence of Lithuanian š. Lycian also assibilated *ḱ to s (*h₁éḱwos > esbe 'horse', *ḱéytor > sijẽni 'lies'), one of the features that groups it with Luwian.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Assibilation, Fronting, Spirantization",
  "languageExamples": [
